  "related_work": "WangZhouSongSherwood2018 already supplies the fixed-level policy-quantile identification logic, so identification is setup here; XiaZhangKong2026 develops successive classification for fixed quantile regimes. OsamaZachariahStoica2020 provides the matching upper-cost-quantile consumer, but its support-based conformal limit does not extrapolate an unbounded rare-loss tail. CarpentierKim2015, specifically Theorems 3--4 and equation (3.6), and BoucheronThomas2015 provide one-tail Hall moduli and threshold tools; coordinatewise familywise use of that machinery yields \\(\\mathcal B_{\\mathrm{CK}}\\), whose strictness under capacity mixing is part of the frontier question. AtheyWager2021, specifically Theorem 1, and KitagawaTetenov2018 treat regular additive policy welfare; their \\(\\sqrt{m/n}\\)-type complexity scale \\(\\mathcal B_{\\mathrm{AW}}\\) is formally separated from moving extreme-tail regret. EinmahlHe2023 studies a predetermined heterogeneous average tail, PanovMorozova2021 studies vanishing heavy impurity, and DaouiaPadoanStupfler2024 studies common-tail pooling; none permits the decision rule to choose mixture components under capacity. SasakiWang2024 supplies a scalar worst-case-bias length principle, HuangLiPeng2025 supplies process inference for fixed treatment pairs and tail levels, and AndrewsKitagawaMcCloskey2024 supplies a regular winner-inference comparison; the explicit paired-cell Hall hypercube here instead forces separation among growing policy mixtures. GuggenbergerMehtaPavlov2026 studies bounded fixed-quantile minimax rules, while WangCaiWangShiTang2026 imposes a linear common-index structure for conditional extreme treatment effects.",
  "technical_internal_limitation": "The baseline paired-splice regret argument controls expected missed-cell count, but exact logarithmic loss is a concave log-sum-exp function of that count. Equal expected mistake counts can yield different expected regrets after unrestricted capacity reallocation, so a wrong-direction Jensen step cannot establish the sharp frontier. For confidence width, the displayed sign-indexed construction is only a route, and its quantitative implications remain unresolved.",
  "honest_scope": "Policy-mixture identification is fixed-level causal setup, not a novelty claim. The fixed-\\(m\\) Hall class, its exact-Pareto member, corrected \\(m^{-1}\\) sorting identity with the \\(m=2\\) arithmetic corollary, finite-policy inversion, Hall-core inversion, dominance map, generic regret sandwich, two-cell rate, and simultaneous confidence system are theorem claims. Selected-policy coverage is a corollary inside the simultaneous theorem. The exact many-cell regret question must classify its relations to both \\(\\mathcal B_{\\mathrm{CK}}\\) and \\(\\mathcal B_{\\mathrm{AW}}\\); the width question must analyze the displayed paired-splice experiment. No common tail index, fixed gap, density, continuous outcome law, nonempty realized cell sample, nuisance-estimator rate, or selection penalty is assumed.",
